<https://ostrails.github.io/assessment-component-metadata-records/metric/FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards.ttl> a ftr:Metric, dqv:Metric, dcat:Resource ;
    dcterms:identifier "https://ostrails.github.io/assessment-component-metadata-records/metric/FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards.ttl"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy "https://ostrails.github.io/assessment-component-metadata-records/metric/FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards.ttl"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    dcat:landingPage "https://ostrails.github.io/assessment-component-metadata-records/metric/FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards.ttl"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    dcterms:title "FAIR Metric - R1.3 - Metadata - Resource adopts community-relevant terminologies or models/formats (Life Science)"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards"^^xsd:string ;
    vivo:abbreviation "FM_R1.3_FS-LS_CommunityStandards"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:description """**What is being measured?**

This metric evaluates whether the database, standard or policy adopts community-relevant terminologies or models/formats for the **Life Science** community. To satisfy this metric, at least one assigned subject must be within the **Life Science** hierarchy of the FAIRsharing Subject Resource Application Ontology (SRAO), and at least one related terminology and/or model/format must have a subject that is identical to or a child of at least one assigned subject within the resource record. In FAIRsharing, this corresponds to terminology artefacts and/or model/format records related via any non-deprecates relationship and curated using the Life Science subject criteria outlined above. Expected input is the DOI or URL of the registry (e.g. FAIRsharing) record under evaluation.

**Why should we measure it?**

R1.3 requires that (meta)data meet domain-relevant community standards. Within the FAIRsharing interpretation of this principle for database-level FAIR evaluation, the focus is on the extent to which resources adopt, support and expose community standards and practices that enable FAIR use of their content. This metric uses the relationships provided within FAIRsharing records to determine whether the resource adopts community-relevant terminologies and/or models/formats for the **Life Science** community. Recognised terminologies and models/formats provide shared approaches for describing, exchanging, interpreting and reusing information. Restricting this metric to the **Life Science** hierarchy creates a domain-specific profile while preserving the same underlying FAIRsharing operationalisation."""^^xsd:string ;
    dcat:keyword "FAIR"^^xsd:string ;
    schema:about "Not applicable"^^xsd:string ;
    ftr:applicationArea <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_4318> ;
    ftr:inDimension <https://w3id.org/fair/principles/terms/R1.3> ;
    dcat:version "1.0.0"^^xsd:string ;
    
    
    ftr:status "Active"@en ;
     
    
    
    
    
